# What a payload in a process-path rootfs reaches when its caller mounted /proc, /sys or
# /dev there, through kavach's public paths: 3.14.7's measurements (ADR-010, and the
# 2026-11-06 process-backend issue's 3.14.7 section). The same binary is the driver and
# the payload, since each rootfs it reads argv in has a /proc. x86-64.
#
#   cyrius build <this file> <dir>/rig-after      # from the repository root
#   cyrius build <this file> <dir>/rig-before     # from a 3.14.6 tree, for the before half
#
# It runs only as real root in a throwaway privileged container, with <dir> bound at /rig:
# the .sh of the same name. Every probe OPENS and never writes, reads /proc/kcore and
# /proc/timer_list for one byte, and opens a block device read-only and closes it.

